# Chana Masala

Based on [https://twosleevers.com/pressure-cooker-homestyle-chana-masala/](https://twosleevers.com/pressure-cooker-homestyle-chana-masala) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20260113120926/https://twosleevers.com/pressure-cooker-homestyle-chana-masala/)) and [https://ministryofcurry.com/instant-pot-chana-masala-recipe/](https://ministryofcurry.com/instant-pot-chana-masala-recipe) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20251207225254/https://ministryofcurry.com/instant-pot-chana-masala-recipe/))

{ rating="0" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

### Chickpeas

- [ ] 1 cup [dried chickpeas]{ ing="dried-chickpeas" }, soaked overnight (or 2x 15 oz cans, drained)
- [ ] 2.5 cups [water]{ ing="water" } (if using dried chickpeas)

### Sauce Base

- [ ] 1 Tbsp [ghee or oil]{ ing="ghee-or-oil" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [cumin seeds]{ ing="cumin-seeds" }
- [ ] 1 large [onion]{ ing="onion" }, finely diced
- [ ] 1 Tbsp [minced ginger]{ ing="minced-ginger" }
- [ ] 4 cloves [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, minced
- [ ] 1 [green chili]{ ing="green-chili" }, minced (or 1/4 tsp cayenne pepper)
- [ ] 2 medium [tomatoes]{ ing="tomatoes" }, chopped (or 1 cup crushed tomatoes)
- [ ] 2 tsp [chana masala spice blend]{ ing="chana-masala-spice-blend" } (or substitute: 1 tsp garam masala + 1/2 tsp ground coriander + 1/2 tsp ground cumin)
- [ ] 1 tsp [ground coriander]{ ing="ground-coriander" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [turmeric powder]{ ing="turmeric-powder" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [red chili powder]{ ing="red-chili-powder" } (adjust to taste)
- [ ] 1 tsp [salt]{ ing="salt" }

### Finishing

- [ ] 1 Tbsp [lemon juice]{ ing="lemon-juice" } (or 1 tsp amchoor/dried mango powder)
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [garam masala]{ ing="garam-masala" }
- [ ] Fresh [cilantro]{ ing="cilantro" }, chopped (for garnish)

### For Serving

- [ ] [Basmati rice]{ ing="basmati-rice" } or naan bread

## Recipe

1. If using [dried chickpeas]{ ing="dried-chickpeas" }, soak overnight in plenty of [water]{ ing="water" }; drain before using. For canned chickpeas, skip to step 4
1. Add soaked [chickpeas]{ ing="dried-chickpeas" } and 2.5 cups [water]{ ing="water" } to Instant Pot
1. Close lid and cook on high pressure for 15-20 minutes; allow natural pressure release for 10 minutes, then quick release remaining pressure
1. Open lid and drain excess liquid, reserving 1 cup of cooking liquid
1. Set Instant Pot to sauté mode and heat [ghee or oil]{ ing="ghee-or-oil" }
1. Add [cumin seeds]{ ing="cumin-seeds" } and let sizzle for 30 seconds until fragrant
1. Add diced [onion]{ ing="onion" } and cook until softened and golden, about 5-7 minutes
1. Add [ginger]{ ing="minced-ginger" }, [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, and [green chili]{ ing="green-chili" }; cook for 1 minute until fragrant
1. Add chopped [tomatoes]{ ing="tomatoes" } and cook until softened, about 3-4 minutes
1. Add [chana masala spice blend]{ ing="chana-masala-spice-blend" }, [coriander]{ ing="ground-coriander" }, turmeric, [chili powder]{ ing="red-chili-powder" }, and [salt]{ ing="salt" }; stir and cook for 1 minute
1. Return cooked [chickpeas]{ ing="dried-chickpeas" } to pot with 1/2-1 cup of reserved cooking liquid
1. Use back of spoon or potato masher to lightly mash some [chickpeas]{ ing="dried-chickpeas" } to thicken sauce
1. Simmer for 5-10 minutes until sauce thickens and [chickpeas]{ ing="dried-chickpeas" } are well-coated
1. Turn off heat and stir in [lemon juice]{ ing="lemon-juice" } and [garam masala]{ ing="garam-masala" }
1. Serve garnished with fresh [cilantro]{ ing="cilantro" }, alongside [rice]{ ing="basmati-rice" } or naan

## Notes

- Serves 4
- Total time: 50 minutes (30 min for chickpeas + 20 min for sauce) plus overnight soaking
- For quick soak: Cover dried chickpeas with boiling water and soak 2 hours
- Using canned chickpeas reduces cook time to 20 minutes
- Vegetarian and can easily be made vegan by using oil instead of ghee
- High in protein (11g per serving) and fiber (14g per serving)
- Nutrition per serving: 260 calories, 34g carbs
- Chana masala spice blend is available at most US grocery stores in the international aisle
- The slight tanginess from lemon juice or amchoor is essential to authentic flavor
